// ===================================================== hashing =============

// ktElemHash (jsrtkotlin.go 4246): hashCode, matching kHash in the interpreter.
//
// The Go twin answers an int64 and EVERY one of its callers - the three top level
// ones and the folds below - takes int32 of it, so the truncation is done here
// once and the answer is always a plain int32. The 64 bit arm is `x ^ (x >>> 32)`
// read as an Int, whose low 32 bits are the XOR of the box's two halves whatever
// the shift's signedness, so sintLo/sintHi give it exactly.
